},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"forStripeError"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/stripeapplepay\/stripecore\/stpapiclient\/pkpaymenterror(forstripeerror:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Converts Stripe errors into the appropriate Apple Pay error, for use in "},{"code":"PKPaymentAuthorizationResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the error can be fixed by the customer within the Apple Pay sheet, we return an NSError that can be displayed in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise, the original error is returned, resulting in the Apple Pay sheet being dismissed. You should display the error message to the customer afterwards."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Currently, we convert billing address related errors into a PKPaymentError that helpfully points to the billing address field in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Note that Apple Pay should prevent most card errors (e.g. invalid CVC, expired cards) when you add a card to the wallet."}]},"doc://com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay/documentation/StripeApplePay/StripeCore/STPAPIClient":{"abstract":[{"text":"STPAPIClient extensions to create Stripe Tokens, Sources, or PaymentMethods from Apple Pay PKPayment objects.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay\/documentation\/StripeApplePay\/StripeCore\/STPAPIClient","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@M@StripeCore@objc(cs)STPAPIClient","text":"STPAPIClient"}],"title":"STPAPIClient","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"STPAPIClient"